@format 1
@id relay.receive-tab
@title Receive relayed tab
@area 6. Relay and routing
@entry input
@summary Restore a startup relay payload or accept a live relay-channel payload as a new selected tab.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related application.startup
@tag relay
@tag tab

@alias app = Cadroue.UIShell.PProgram
@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow

[input] Relay payload is supplied <input>
> source

[source] Identify the delivery path <decision>
? "Application starts with a relay argument" > startup
? "A relay channel payload arrives" > live

[startup] Read a startup relay payload <process>
- Read and clear the startup relay file @ app.LRelayStartupRead(...)
> place

[place] Place the startup window <process>
- Apply the relayed window position before restoring its tab @ window.PWindowRelayPlace(...)
> accept

[live] A relay channel payload arrives <input>
- Receive a live delivery from the process relay channel @ window.PWindowRelayHandle(...)
> activate

[accept] Restore relayed tab <process>
- Add a tab with the relayed layout, output preset, and custom name @ window.PWindowRelayAccept(...)
- Select the new tab and apply relayed media, sections, and list state @ window.PWindowRelayAccept(...)
> result

[activate] Restore and present live delivery <process>
- Accept the delivered tab on the UI dispatcher @ window.PWindowRelayHandle(...)
- Restore the window when minimized and activate it @ window.PWindowRelayHandle(...)
> result

[result] Relayed tab available <output>
= The relayed tab is open and selected in the receiving process.
